---
import InnerPageLayout from "../../layouts/InnerPageLayout.astro";
import MetaMeasurementConsent from "../../components/MetaMeasurementConsent.astro";
---

<InnerPageLayout
  title="Privacy | George B. Johnson"
  description="Read the privacy policy for georgebjohnson.com, including site analytics, optional Builders Lab Meta measurement, link attribution, hosting, and external links."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  eyebrow="Site policy"
  heading="Privacy"
  lead="This site does not currently collect email addresses through a form. It uses site analytics and offers an optional Meta measurement choice on Builders Lab."
  currentPage="Privacy"
>
  <section class="policy-content section-pad" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
    <div class="section-label"><span>01</span><span>Privacy policy</span></div>
    <div class="prose prose-wide">
      <h2 id="policy-title">How this site handles data</h2>
      <p><strong>Last updated: July 31, 2026.</strong></p>
      <p>This policy applies to <a href="/">georgebjohnson.com</a>.</p>

      <h3>Information submitted to this site</h3>
      <p>This site does not currently provide an email signup form, account registration, comments, or checkout. It does not ask you to submit a name, email address, mailing address, or payment information.</p>

      <h3>Technical delivery</h3>
      <p>Like other websites, the hosting and content-delivery providers used to serve this site may process technical request data, such as an IP address, browser information, requested URL, and timestamp, for delivery, reliability, and security.</p>

      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>This site uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors find and use the site. It may collect information such as pages viewed, visit timing, referring pages, approximate location, and browser or device details. Google Analytics may also use first-party cookies or similar technologies to distinguish visits. This information helps evaluate site performance and improve the content. Analytics page locations and referrers are configured without URL query strings.</p>
      <p>Google processes this information under its own privacy terms. For more details, read <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>. Google also provides a <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>
      <p>This site also uses Cloudflare Web Analytics for aggregate page-view and performance information. Cloudflare automatically adds its analytics script when it serves the site and receives the resulting measurement request. Cloudflare states that Web Analytics does not use cookies, local storage, or fingerprinting to track visitors across sites. Read <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare’s Web Analytics information</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h3>Builders Lab links and campaign attribution</h3>
      <p>Builders Lab buttons lead to the current membership page on Skool. When a visitor arrives through an advertisement, the site may preserve a limited set of campaign details and advertising click identifiers in the link to Skool so the visit can be attributed. Unknown, malformed, conflicting, or destination-changing information is discarded.</p>
      <p>This site does not save those click identifiers or include them in its Google Analytics events. Skool receives only the retained attribution details after you choose to follow the link, and Skool’s own privacy practices then apply.</p>

      <h3 id="meta-measurement">Optional Meta measurement on Builders Lab</h3>
      <p>Meta measurement is limited to the Builders Lab page and does not load unless you choose <strong>Allow Meta measurement</strong>. After an affirmative choice, the page can send one page-view event and record which of the two Builders Lab join buttons you selected. These events do not show that you reached Skool, registered, joined, or paid for a membership.</p>
      <p>Meta may receive technical information needed to deliver and measure these events, such as an IP address, browser or device information, referrer information, and cookie or similar identifiers created by Meta’s browser tool. Before Meta measurement loads, this site removes the landing page query string from the visible browser address. It does not intentionally add names, email addresses, phone numbers, payment details, destination URLs, campaign parameters, click identifiers, membership status, value, or currency to Meta events.</p>
      <p>Your Meta measurement choice is stored only in this browser for up to six months with the choice, notice version, decision time, and expiry time. Rejecting does not affect the page or its links. Use the persistent <strong>Privacy choices</strong> control to change your preference. Withdrawing stops future site-originated Meta measurement after the page reloads; it does not retract information already received by Meta. Read <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/">Meta’s Privacy Policy</a> for information about Meta’s processing and privacy choices.</p>

      <h3>Controller contact and privacy requests</h3>
      <p>George B. Johnson, sole proprietor, is responsible for this site’s handling of the choices and events described above. For privacy questions or rights requests, email <a href="mailto:privacy@georgebjohnson.com">privacy@georgebjohnson.com</a>.</p>

      <h3>Fonts</h3>
      <p>This site serves its typeface files from the same domain. Loading the site’s fonts does not require your browser to connect to Google Fonts or another font-delivery service.</p>

      <h3>External links</h3>
      <p>This site links to services operated by other organizations, including LinkedIn, YouTube, Skool, Amazon, and George Digital. Those sites have their own privacy practices. Their policies apply after you follow an external link.</p>

      <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
      <p>This page may be updated if the site adds new features or changes the services used to deliver it. The date above identifies the latest published version.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <MetaMeasurementConsent />
  <script>
    import { initMetaMeasurementConsent } from "../../scripts/builders-lab-meta.js";
    initMetaMeasurementConsent(window, document, { enableMeasurement: false });
  </script>
</InnerPageLayout>
